WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.500
Each danger has a guard.

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.050
An approver might approve a
request that breaks the standard,

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.713
so the check runs before approval, and
Chapter 6 refuses a write without a request.

4
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:14.888
A group managed account created by hand
is caught by the drift rule on every run.

5
00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:20.102
If SailPoint correlates no owner, or
the wrong one, certifications go astray,

6
00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:23.662
so that's a finding, and one
attribute names one owner.

7
00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:26.525
A certification by a
non-owner doesn't count.

8
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:31.475
A disabled account is deleted only
after ninety quiet days, by a person.

9
00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:34.277
And because the import
formats could drift from

10
00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:37.010
the products' exports,
every header is checked.
